From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:00:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: fold the inline angle wraps into AngleWrap180

The wrap of an angle into [-180, 180] is written out as "x * (1/360)",
"floor(+ 0.5)", "* 360" all over the game code. com_math.h gains
AngleWrap180() with that body, and the 19 copies that do it in float
call it, AngleSubtract() among them.

Results do not change: each folded form was compared with the helper
over every float input. Not folded: the copies that multiply in double
or add a double 0.5 before the floor, which differ for some inputs, and
the single-player actor and turret copies whose decompiled shape is not
plain enough to match. AngleNormalize180() is left alone; it uses fmodf
and rounds differently, so calling it would change results. Second
half of upstream issue 45.
